"I don't want any unnecessary casualties. I don't mean to underestimate the soldiers' training, but neither do I intend to look down on any of you. That is also why I accepted this mission."

"For our sake... so that we would not hurt the soldiers?"

"Also, to prevent a situation where you all get hurt. I can ensure that."

Reinhard replied to Rem, who had continued the exchange in place of the now-silent Otto. The moment that answer was given, the sensation of the world breaking out in goosebumps raced through the royal capital.

Reinhard's will, his conviction, was conveyed almost painfully.

However, yet, it was completely and utterly out of the question.

"――I've been shuttin' my trap and listenin' to Otto-nii and Rem talk for a damn while now, but there's somethin' in what yer sayin' that I just can't nod along with, oi."

"Can't nod along with?"

Cracking the bones of his fists, Garfiel equipped the silver gauntlets onto his arms. He ground his fangs with a "Yeah" at the Sword Saint, who narrowed his eyes at Garfiel's stance.

He understood Reinhard's intention in coming alone to apprehend them.

The thought of not wanting any unnecessary injuries was something Garfiel agreed with.

Even so, he didn't like it.

Because...

"Seems for someone who ain't lookin' down, yer missin' one little thought up there. ――The thought that right here! You! Are gonna get the shit beaten outta ya! By ME!"

In an instant, Garfiel roared and sprang from the street, lunging at Reinhard.

What flickered in Reinhard's eyes as he watched Garfiel charge was not surprise or caution.

"――――"

What flickered was the pained color of accepting Garfiel's decision.

A look of pity, as if watching a child who broke a vase, not apologize to their parents, but bury the shards under the dirt.

His eyes carrying that grievous color, Reinhard faced Garfiel, who was slamming his fist down upon him.

It was the same form as the first time Garfiel had encountered Reinhard in Priestella, when, overwhelmed by his very presence, he had pounced as a conditioned reflex.

Reinhard raised his right arm against Garfiel's crashing blow. Those five spread fingers would catch the fierce fist, easily parrying it...

"――!?"

...did not happen.

"OOOOOOHHHH――!!"

Roaring, Garfiel put his entire body into motion, forcibly refusing to let the force be diverted outward. The impact exploded against Reinhard's receiving arm, the sleeve of the Sword Saint's white clothes burst, and the energy that could not be deflected sent spiderweb cracks racing beneath his feet.

And to Reinhard, whose eyes widened at a blow beyond his expectations, Garfiel let out a "Ha!" and laughed, baring his fangs.

"Don't go thinkin' everyone else is always gonna be totterin' along behind ya!!"

His dropkick, launched with his folded knees fully extended, slammed into the center of Reinhard's crossed arms, and the resulting shockwave raged ferociously through a corner of the royal capital.

――He felt as if he could hear the world clapping its hands in triumphant delight at the start of the battle.



