In that instant, Garfiel and Wilhelm's gazes crossed, and instinct knew.

And Garfiel accepted Wilhelm's decision, welcomed it.

The "Sword Demon's" resolute will, his answer was—

"――It can't be."

The answer took visible form, and Reinhard's eyes were dyed with shock.

"That is a bad habit of yours. Misjudging the measure of another's resolve."

Those blue eyes of Wilhelm, as serene as a lake surface, fixed upon that shock and declared.

The unleashed sword light traced a semicircle as it was delivered―slicing open the flank of the raised Garfiel, the blade passing through and deeply cutting the leg of Reinhard.

"About... damn time it reached ya...!"

Truly, cutting flesh to sever bone—the experience of having fought back-to-back in Priestella served here for Garfiel and Wilhelm's wordless coordination.

To Reinhard's senses, if Garfiel had cut into the sword's trajectory, Wilhelm should have stopped his attack. But the "Sword Demon" did not do so, instead grasping the purpose Garfiel and the others had to achieve.

Therefore, trusting in Garfiel's regenerative power, he cut through Garfiel to cut Reinhard.

"――Tch"

Garfiel slipped free from the arm of Reinhard, who had suffered a deep wound to his leg and choked back his breath.

Pressing a hand to the wound in his side, Garfiel activated healing magic while keeping his consciousness from flying away. Though feeling a subtle difficulty in the activation, he poured his entire effort into emergency first aid.

"Well done."

Then, before the freed Garfiel could fall to the ground, Wilhelm's extending arm caught his body. Looking, Wilhelm had already sheathed the twin swords in both hands, and in the arm opposite the one holding Garfiel, he carried the collapsed Otto.

Holding the two of them just as they were, Wilhelm glanced at Reinhard,

"Even for you, that wound will not heal in an instant."

"Grandfather, please wait! They, and Crusch-sama are—"

"I cannot entrust my sword to the Kingdom as it is now."

"――!"

Responding to the voice holding him back, Wilhelm leapt a great distance backward.

Left behind, Reinhard's eyes widened, but just as Wilhelm had pointed out, the deeply slashed wound on his leg was severe; even he could not move immediately.

"Rem-dono, you have awakened! The young ladies!"

"Yes! Unknown old man!"

In that interval, responding to Wilhelm's call, Rem swiftly turned and ran to Petra and Meili, scooping up their startled bodies with a "Kya!"

Watching this from the corner of his eye, Otto, slung over Wilhelm's shoulder, stirred slightly,

"Follow the wall, head west...!"

"Otto-san! You're alive—"

"I am alive...! To the west, there's no sound or presence of insects. ―They can't deceive me there."

"――Understood."

On the premise that his Divine Protection of the Voice of Spirits was being exploited, Otto deliberately chose to escape in a direction where he couldn't hear the voices of living things, thus avoiding any trickery.

Following that instruction, Wilhelm exchanged a nod with Rem, and they began to run from that place at full speed, attempting to flee and leave Reinhard upon the battlefield.

"――――"

Violently shaken within the arms of the "Sword Demon," Garfiel somehow managed to move his neck and looked at the corner of the royal capital, which had been reduced to a wretched sight in just a short time, and at Reinhard left behind there.

He had his thoughts on the matter. It wasn't that he hated Reinhard.

And yet, for having overcome him, the obstacle who was incompatible with their choice in this place, there was relief and a sense of accomplishment—

"――Even so, I am the Kingdom's sword."

At that moment, Garfiel felt the world hold its breath.

Not stop breathing, but hold its breath. ―Because, along with a quiet stirring of the atmosphere, the "Dragon Sword" Reid, its legendary blade laid bare, emitted a cold, pale blue radiance.

△▼△▼△▼△

―The "Dragon Sword" Reid.

One of the ten Magic Swords and Holy Swords that exist in the world, it is a legendary sword permitted to be wielded only by the "Sword Saint" of the Dragon Kingdom of Lugunica, passed down through generations.

While its immense hidden power is rumored, the sword's nature of choosing when it should be drawn means that opportunities for its actual use are hardly ever known; it is considered a sword with a history.

Especially since coming into the hands of the current "Sword Saint," Reinhard van Astrea, the occasions the "Dragon Sword" has been used have decreased drastically. The stories where it was definitively drawn can be counted on the fingers of one hand.

This is, without a doubt, because the transcendent ability of its owner, Reinhard, relegates any opponent he faces as unworthy of drawing the "Dragon Sword."

In fact, in many instances where Reinhard was called upon to act as the "Sword Saint," the immense power of the "Dragon Sword" Reid was never necessary.

For that reason, the "Dragon Sword" Reid was assessed by Natsuki Subaru as, "Isn't he stronger just swinging it around like an absolutely unbreakable blunt weapon?", which left a wry smile on Reinhard's face.

However―

"――――"

Once the blade of the "Dragon Sword" is even revealed, the world recognizes it as a grave matter.

The conditions for the "Dragon Sword" Reid to be drawn are shrouded in mystery, even for those well-versed in the history of Lugunica, and even for the successive generations of the "Sword Saint" family who possess it. Whether it is the strength of the enemy, the weight of what is borne, or the ferocity of the danger faced—none correspond to the answer.

If there is one thing that can be said for certain, it is that when the "Dragon Sword" Reid is drawn, there has never been a time when its purpose went unfulfilled.

"――――"

As if their whole bodies had been doused with a cold wave, their minds and bodies, struck by that sword aura, trembled.

No. No. No. No. No. No. No. No. No.

That, absolutely, must not be allowed to be swung.

"――Tch"

A clicking sound rang out; the teeth of Garfiel, held by the old swordsman who had interposed himself, had chattered. Held as he was, he too looked at Reinhard, even though he shouldn't have, and witnessed the drawn "Dragon Sword," feeling a sensation that made his hair stand on end.

Rem and the old swordsman, with no leeway to look back, must have sensed it on their backs, or perhaps passing through them entirely, the density of the sword aura released by the very soul itself.

But even so, they desperately refused to be paralyzed by fear and did what had to be done.

He honestly thought that was amazing. He was impressed.

He couldn't do that. Without an example to follow, how could they do it?

So, taking them as an example, he would do what had to be done. ―She would surely be angry with him, though.

He would do what had to be done.

Because he wanted to stand alongside those who always lived like that, giving their all, as examples to follow—

"――Come on out, Sand Earthworm-chan!!"

The next instant, a sensation that shook the ground, literally and without exaggeration, rocked the royal capital.

"Meili-chan!?"

Petra, who had been held in Rem's arms, searching for something to resist the "Dragon Sword," opened her eyes wide, staring in shock at Meili, who had broken her warning.

To Petra's gaze, Meili stuck out her tongue and said, "Sorry, yes."

"I know that if I do this, it'll cause trouble for Subaru-brother and Emilia-sister... but, we can't end it here, right?"

"―You, idiot! Idiot, idiot! After you'd finally been forgiven...!"

"Oh, so that was Petra-chan's..."

With tears in her eyes, understanding dawned on Meili at Petra's repeated cries of "idiot."

That calling magical beasts as the "Magical Beast User" Meili risked making the danger of the Emilia Camp known to a greater degree was only one part of the reason. What Petra had truly wanted to prevent was a situation where the Kingdom would once again view Meili—who had served as a guide to the Pleiades Watchtower, and who had been forgiven for her past as a dangerous assassin—as a threat.

"It's fine, yes. ...Because I got to see a dream, even if just for a little while."

Perhaps, she thought, her sins might be forgiven and she might walk a proper path.

In fact, she had even imagined walking such a future together with the people who were kind to her.

That was enough. Because her heart had become as warm as it was when she was with that troublesome older sister.

―Because she had seen such a dream.

"Sword Saint big brother, can you chase after us? I've put four Sand Earthworms at the east, west, south, and north gates of the royal capital. They're all in a huge panic right about now, yes?"

They were Sand Earthworms of the Auguria Dunes, incomparably larger than any other.

To this trump card she had commanded to follow secretly and kept hidden beneath the royal capital, Meili deliberately gave instructions through her Divine Protection of Demon Manipulation, inciting fear in a showy manner.

If Reinhard didn't go, there might be victims. ―Meili didn't particularly care if there were.

As long as the people here, as long as Subaru, Beatrice, and Emilia weren't hurt.

Anyone other than those who cherished her, and those she wanted to cherish, could die, for all she cared.

"――Meili"

In the distance, she saw the lips of Reinhard, who held the "Dragon Sword," move.

Meili was also in the position of having crossed over to the Pleiades Watchtower together with Reinhard and Felt. They had time together, and she remembered him showing concern for her.

Even so, it couldn't compare to Subaru and the others.

"I'm a bad kid, after all."

So she spoke, with a mocking smile, waving a small hand at Reinhard.

From the corner of her eye, a drop heavy with heat spilled over and traced down her cheek, but Meili herself did not notice. The ones who noticed were the "Sword Saint," whose eyes saw with clarity even across the vast distance growing between them, and Petra, held by the desperately running Rem, weeping at her friend's decision.

"Meili-chan, you idiot...! I'm sorry, I'm sorry...!"

To her weeping friend's great decision, the girl's tearful, apologetic voice fell away futilely.

And at the end of that immense, immense choice―

"――――"

―For the first time since the "Dragon Sword" Reid came into the hands of the "Sword Saint" Reinhard van Astrea, the sword was returned to its scabbard without fulfilling the purpose for which it was drawn.
